  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b769da97cc9c62c4c9115b0b03ad86d2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dad's Journal
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  pages:
  - 'Journal Entry 2:


    I haven''t told Miguel what''s been happening. I can''t
    bring myself to involve him. I''m terrified this thing will come after my eldest
    son too. Whatever this is, it ends with me.


    I went back to the salesman.
    I lost control. Beat him bloody right there in his own shop, screaming at him
    to take it back. He swore he couldn''t undo it. Said there was only one way to
    get rid of it. A ritual.


    Six candles. The doll placed in the centre of
    the house, right there in the foyer. That''s how I banish the spirit.


    Light
    is the only thing that keeps it away. But it knows that. Every time I get close
    to keeping the house lit, it sabotages me. Drains the generator, destroys the
    electrical box, even snaps the main lever clean off.


    I bought a whole box
    of spare levers. I''m down to my last one now. I''ve locked it away upstairs
    and padlocked it in a box. '
  - "Journal Entry 3:\n\nI managed to source a spare breaker lever and secured it
    inside a locked tool box nearby. I was planning to make one final attempt tonight.
    I misplaced the note where I wrote down the combination, but that doesn't matter,
    the numbers are burned into my memory anyway. The problem is no matter where
    I hide that grotesque piece of wood and cloth, whether locked in the shed or
    thrown under the garage workbench, it always finds its way back into Sammy\u2019s
    room. Over the last two days, its behavior has turned wildly erratic. Door handles
    rattle on their own, the temperature plunges, and the shadows in the hallways
    stretch toward us when we turn our backs."
  - "Journal Entry 4:\n\nWe can\u2019t fight this anymore. We are packing whatever
    fits in the trunk of the car tonight and running. Let it keep the house. Let
    it keep everything I worked for. I just need my wife and my sons alive. "
  triggersObjective: 0
